<h3 data-start=3D"2290" data-end=3D"2310" class=3D"">Key Differences:</h3>
<ol data-start=3D"2311" data-end=3D"2971">
<li data-start=3D"2311" data-end=3D"2613" class=3D"" style=3D"">
<p data-start=3D"2314" data-end=3D"2613" class=3D""><strong data-start=3D"2=
314" data-end=3D"2327">Structure</strong>: In Java, code resides within cla=
sses, and the entry point for execution is the <code data-start=3D"2408" da=
ta-end=3D"2414">main</code> method inside the class. In Python, code can ru=
n directly from top-level statements without needing to be inside a class o=
r method (though you can organize it inside functions or classes if needed)=
.</p>
</li>
<li data-start=3D"2618" data-end=3D"2847" class=3D"" style=3D"">
<p data-start=3D"2621" data-end=3D"2847" class=3D""><strong data-start=3D"2=
621" data-end=3D"2656">Static Typing vs Dynamic Typing</strong>: Java is st=
atically typed, meaning that the type of a variable is known at compile tim=
e (e.g., <code data-start=3D"2752" data-end=3D"2757">int</code>, <code data=
-start=3D"2759" data-end=3D"2767">String</code>), whereas Python is dynamic=
ally typed, meaning types are determined at runtime.</p>
</li>
<li data-start=3D"2849" data-end=3D"2971" class=3D"" style=3D"">
<p data-start=3D"2852" data-end=3D"2971" class=3D""><strong data-start=3D"2=
852" data-end=3D"2862">Syntax</strong>: Java uses semicolons to terminate s=
tatements (<code data-start=3D"2910" data-end=3D"2913">;</code>), while Pyt=
hon uses indentation to define blocks of code.</p>
</li>
</ol>
<p data-start=3D"2973" data-end=3D"3330" class=3D"">In summary, in Java, yo=
u need to encapsulate everything in classes and methods. Even if you're jus=
t writing a simple program that accepts user input, it's done inside a clas=
s and the <code data-start=3D"3156" data-end=3D"3162">main</code> method. I=
n contrast, Python offers more flexibility in this regard, allowing you to =
write code more freely without the necessity of wrapping everything inside =
classes.</p></div></div></div></div><div class=3D"flex absolute right-0 lef=
