-oriented programming (OOP)</strong> language. The class-based structure is=
 central to Java's core principles of OOP, which aim to make programs easie=
r to understand, maintain, and extend. Let me explain why Java adopts this =
approach and how it aligns with key OOP principles:</p>
<h3 data-start=3D"372" data-end=3D"425" class=3D"">1. <strong data-start=3D=
"379" data-end=3D"425">Encapsulation (Data and Behavior Together)</strong><=
/h3>
<p data-start=3D"426" data-end=3D"590" class=3D"">In OOP, <strong data-star=
t=3D"434" data-end=3D"451">encapsulation</strong> is the principle of bundl=
ing data (variables) and the methods (functions) that operate on the data i=
nto a single unit called a <strong data-start=3D"579" data-end=3D"588">clas=
s</strong>.</p>
<ul data-start=3D"592" data-end=3D"816">
<li data-start=3D"592" data-end=3D"816" class=3D"" style=3D"">
<p data-start=3D"594" data-end=3D"625" class=3D""><strong data-start=3D"594=
" data-end=3D"623">Benefits of Encapsulation</strong>:</p>
<ul data-start=3D"628" data-end=3D"816">
<li data-start=3D"628" data-end=3D"698" class=3D"" style=3D"">
<p data-start=3D"630" data-end=3D"698" class=3D"">Protects the internal sta=
te of an object from external modification.</p>
</li>
<li data-start=3D"701" data-end=3D"741" class=3D"" style=3D"">
<p data-start=3D"703" data-end=3D"741" class=3D"">Makes code more organized=
 and modular.</p>
</li>
<li data-start=3D"744" data-end=3D"816" class=3D"" style=3D"">
<p data-start=3D"746" data-end=3D"816" class=3D"">Helps manage complexity b=
y keeping related data and behavior together.</p>
</li>
</ul>
</li>
</ul>
<p data-start=3D"818" data-end=3D"869" class=3D"">For example, in Java, a c=
lass might look like this:</p>
