<h3 data-start=3D"2446" data-end=3D"2487" class=3D"">3. <strong data-start=
=3D"2453" data-end=3D"2487">Inheritance (Code Reusability)</strong></h3>
<p data-start=3D"2488" data-end=3D"2732" class=3D"">Java supports <strong d=
ata-start=3D"2502" data-end=3D"2517">inheritance</strong>, a key OOP featur=
e, which allows a new class to inherit the properties and behaviors (method=
s) of an existing class. This encourages <strong data-start=3D"2651" data-e=
nd=3D"2671">code reusability</strong> and establishes a natural hierarchy b=
etween related classes.</p>
<ul data-start=3D"2734" data-end=3D"2924">
<li data-start=3D"2734" data-end=3D"2924" class=3D"" style=3D"">
<p data-start=3D"2736" data-end=3D"2764" class=3D""><strong data-start=3D"2=
736" data-end=3D"2763">Benefits of Inheritance</strong>:</p>
<ul data-start=3D"2767" data-end=3D"2924">
<li data-start=3D"2767" data-end=3D"2828" class=3D"" style=3D"">
<p data-start=3D"2769" data-end=3D"2828" class=3D"">Reduces code duplicatio=
n by reusing code from base classes.</p>
</li>
<li data-start=3D"2831" data-end=3D"2874" class=3D"" style=3D"">
<p data-start=3D"2833" data-end=3D"2874" class=3D"">Makes code easier to ma=
intain and extend.</p>
</li>
<li data-start=3D"2877" data-end=3D"2924" class=3D"" style=3D"">
<p data-start=3D"2879" data-end=3D"2924" class=3D"">Allows for polymorphism=
 (more on that below).</p>
</li>
</ul>
</li>
</ul>
<p data-start=3D"2926" data-end=3D"3088" class=3D"">For example, if you hav=
e a general class <code data-start=3D"2967" data-end=3D"2975">Animal</code>=
, you can create more specific classes, like <code data-start=3D"3020" data=
-end=3D"3025">Dog</code> and <code data-start=3D"3030" data-end=3D"3035">Ca=
t</code>, which inherit properties and methods from <code data-start=3D"307=
9" data-end=3D"3087">Animal</code>.</p>
