<h3 data-start=3D"3505" data-end=3D"3560" class=3D"">4. <strong data-start=
=3D"3512" data-end=3D"3560">Polymorphism (Flexibility and Extensibility)</s=
trong></h3>
<p data-start=3D"3561" data-end=3D"3788" class=3D"">Java=E2=80=99s <strong =
data-start=3D"3568" data-end=3D"3584">polymorphism</strong> allows objects =
of different classes to be treated as objects of a common superclass. This =
leads to flexibility in code and the ability to extend and modify behavior =
easily without changing existing code.</p>
<ul data-start=3D"3790" data-end=3D"3973">
<li data-start=3D"3790" data-end=3D"3973" class=3D"" style=3D"">
<p data-start=3D"3792" data-end=3D"3821" class=3D""><strong data-start=3D"3=
792" data-end=3D"3820">Benefits of Polymorphism</strong>:</p>
<ul data-start=3D"3824" data-end=3D"3973">
<li data-start=3D"3824" data-end=3D"3878" class=3D"" style=3D"">
<p data-start=3D"3826" data-end=3D"3878" class=3D"">Allows you to write mor=
e flexible and reusable code.</p>
</li>
<li data-start=3D"3881" data-end=3D"3973" class=3D"" style=3D"">
<p data-start=3D"3883" data-end=3D"3973" class=3D"">Enables one interface t=
o be used for different underlying forms (e.g., different classes).</p>
</li>
</ul>
</li>
</ul>
<p data-start=3D"3975" data-end=3D"4143" class=3D"">In Java, polymorphism a=
llows you to use the same method name across different classes, and the cor=
rect method will be called based on the actual object type at runtime.</p>
